# Copy to .env and fill in for local runs:  cp .env.sample .env
# .env is gitignored; never commit real keys. Read by scripts/chat_appsci_user_sim.py (and any local run).
# These are the operator-facing model config; the agent-facing HTTP contract is docs/user_simulator_api.md.
#
# INTERNAL (gateway): you usually don't edit model creds here at all -- run `gateway login` once, then
# `source the setup steps in README.md`, which maps ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL/ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN onto MODEL_* and
# APPSCI_AGENT_* for you. (Slides eval data is vendored via Git LFS now; the S3/AWS vars below are
# maintainer-only, for refreshing that vendored copy — not needed to run anything.)


# Barebone first-party API: leave MODEL_API_KEY unset and set the provider-standard key, which
# LiteLLM reads itself:
#   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
#   OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
#
# Any gateway/proxy (incl. an internal endpoint): point at it with a base_url + bearer token.
#   MODEL_BASE_URL=https://your-gateway/v1
#   MODEL_API_KEY=<token>
# (Internal: `eval "$(gateway env)"` exports GATEWAY_TOKEN / ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL; map those
#  into MODEL_API_KEY / MODEL_BASE_URL in your launch script -- the benchmark itself is gateway-free.)
#
# Optional extra HTTP headers for that gateway, as one or more `Name: Value` lines. gateway uses
# X-Gateway-User for per-user identity/attribution and can reject a request without it
# (403 identity_required); setup_local_with_gateway.sh maps ANTHROPIC_CUSTOM_HEADERS here for you.
#   MODEL_CUSTOM_HEADERS=X-Gateway-User: you@example.com

# --- Artifact agent user sim model (EVAL-time sim; pinned to a different provider on purpose) ---
# The eval-time sim that drives a multi_turn task's conversation against the finished artifact is
# pinned to tau-bench's user-simulator model (tau2-bench's DEFAULT_LLM_USER) so eval-time user
# behavior stays comparable to the benchmark our tasks are converted from. The BUILD-time appsci
# agent user sim above stays on Claude via MODEL_*. Default below is the built-in one -- shown, not
# required; this is the ONLY var for this sim.
#   ARTIFACT_USERSIM_MODEL=openai/gpt-5.2
# Auth has no dedicated vars: LiteLLM reads the provider-standard OPENAI_* ones, and
# MODEL_API_KEY / MODEL_BASE_URL are NOT inherited (the Anthropic gateway is the wrong endpoint for an
# openai/ model id).
#   OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# INTERNAL (gateway): the gateway does serve gpt-5.2 -- `gateway models --provider openai` lists
# openai-gpt-5.2 -- over an OpenAI-compatible endpoint at $ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL/v1. setup_local_with_gateway.sh
# maps that for you (OPENAI_BASE_URL + OPENAI_API_KEY + ARTIFACT_USERSIM_MODEL=openai/openai-gpt-5.2);
# the gateway doesn't know the first-party snapshot id, hence its own alias.
# Pointing this at a DIFFERENT model (e.g. a Claude id) works but is no longer tau-bench-comparable --
# fine for local debugging, don't report those scores.

# --- Applied-science agent auth (provider-neutral) ---
# Non-auth settings (model, max_turns, etc.) are configured via YAML/JSON config files.
#
# First-party Anthropic API: just set ANTHROPIC_API_KEY above, leave these unset.
#
# Gateway/proxy: set both base_url + token.
#   APPSCI_AGENT_BASE_URL=https://your-gateway/v1
#   APPSCI_AGENT_API_KEY=<token>
#
# Same optional gateway headers, for the agent's own LLM calls (agent loop + mini-swe-agent).
#   APPSCI_AGENT_CUSTOM_HEADERS=X-Gateway-User: you@example.com
#
# Fireworks (an open-source / hosted model as the agent under test): a first-party provider to
# LiteLLM, so a key is the ONLY credential -- LiteLLM resolves the endpoint from the model id's
# `fireworks_ai/` prefix, and there is no base URL to set.
#   FIREWORKS_API_KEY=fw_...
# Name the model where the agent's model is chosen, NOT here: `agent_model:` in your run_tasks config
# (or `--agent-model` / a sweep's `agent_model:` matrix axis), e.g.
#   agent_model: fireworks_ai/accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k3
# The three APPSCI_AGENT_ vars above must be UNSET for such a run: they are the endpoint, token and
# headers the agent's own calls use, and they outrank the provider the model id names. A leftover
# gateway URL with no token beside it is refused outright, because it would send the FIREWORKS key to
# that endpoint as the bearer token. `source scripts/setup_local_with_fireworks.sh` sets the model and
# clears all three for you.
# Only the agent under test moves to Fireworks -- MODEL_* (build sim + judges) and
# ARTIFACT_USERSIM_MODEL stay as they are, which is what keeps scores comparable across model arms.
# That is by construction, not just by convention: no Fireworks key is forwarded into the build-time
# sim's container, so pointing APPSCI_USERSIM_MODEL at a fireworks_ai/ id will not work.
#
# Per-request LiteLLM timeout in seconds (optional, default 120). Bounds a single model call so a
# hung/throttled gateway request fails fast (and is retried) instead of parking on LiteLLM's 6000s
# default. Raise it if long completions hit false timeouts. Applies to the agent loop + mini-swe-agent.
#   APPSCI_LLM_TIMEOUT_S=120

# --- NOT set here (runtime wiring) ---
# APPSCI_USERSIM_TOKEN / APPSCI_USERSIM_SPEC_PATH / APPSCI_USERSIM_PERSONA_PATH / APPSCI_USERSIM_URL are set automatically by the
# orchestrator (or by scripts/chat_appsci_user_sim.py from its --task/--persona flags). Don't put them here.
